ly disapperate somewhere else at  that moment  we all know robert pattinson has some  very strong feelings about his time  on twilight and to be fair he put up  with quite a bit of what some people  would probably call ridiculousness  however he finally reached his breaking  point when it came to renesmee's birth  scene in breaking dawn  he claims having to actually bite  through a weird prosthetic that was  covered in fake blood  was the hardest scene he filmed in the  entire franchise  i think that was the major the major  factor  we just have one word to say about that  ew  getting to film in hungary might seem  like a dream but the shadow and bone  cast are admitting that  while it was beautiful a lot of the time  it was rough  most of the weather conditions you see  going on in the show were a hundred  percent real  especially the sleet and thunderstorms  now imagine having to spend hours on end  enduring these conditions pretty uh  pretty terrifying  actors danielle galligan and callahan  skogman said the cherry on top was  having to film in a cold water tank  during these conditions  cherry deals with much heavier content  than tom holland is used to filming for  marvel  which made the whole process of filming  the movie difficult  the war scenes in particular are very  overwhelming and require so many pieces  to fit together  needless to say tom was challenged and  said this  role took me to some of the darkest  places i have ever been  emotionally physically anythingly he  even  almost broke his nose while filming so  i'm yeah i'm really really proud of this  movie  the after series is steamy but behind  the scenes  we guess you can say the steaminess  evaporates  we all know this iconic lake scene  between tessa and hardin right  well for actor hiro finds tiffin that  scene was  suffocating literally he wasn't able to  touch the floor in the lake which meant  he was struggling to keep afloat and  not drown while also trying to give his  best performance  you think that's weird no  if they sound a little out of breath  during the scene it's because they were  in the end many toe cramps later they  managed to get it done  we've heard of actors having to go on  strict diets to get in shape for a film  but for this role in the witcher henry  cavill had to dehydrate himself  you heard us the actor essentially gave  up water for four days in order to film  shirtless scenes  like this one in the bathtub it's a very  iconic moment  supposedly it helped him seem like he  had more muscle definition  it got so bad by the fourth day that he  said he could actually smell nearby  water  i was surprised that i still existed  just watching the battle of the bastards  in game of thrones was  tense but for kit harington it was one  of the most  challenging scenes he ever had to shoot  in his role as jon snow  they had to rehearse the scene for weeks  because the battle was one long  continuous take  which means everything had to go  perfectly  as you could imagine it took hours and  hours we're exhausted just thinking  about it  it feels good to be alive sometimes it  isn't wild set locations or epic stunts  that make things  difficult to film sometimes it's just  baking  we're sorry to burst your bubble but to  all the boys lara jean  is far from a good baker in real life  lana condor has explained how difficult  those baking scenes were for her  because she had no experience in order  to get through it they had to hire a  professional baker to stand next to her  and instruct her on what to do and how  to do it  just so it could pass as convincing on  screen  it was a educational experience  you'd assume that the hard scenes to  film for brie larson and captain marvel  would be some intense stunts  but that couldn't be further from the  truth her most challenging scenes were  the ones she had to film with her furry  friend  goose great team partner gave a lot brie  is highly allergic to cats  so you can just imagine how she must  have been filming on those days  but brie was able to find humor in the  situation it was kind of like the  ongoing joke that like  i would do like crazy wire work stunts  but then the cat showed up on set and i  was like  we need to have a plan i'd be like  stressed out like washing my hands a  million times  believe it or not the actual heist  scenes in money heist were a piece of  cake to film for the actors in  comparison to their season 3 adventure  on a boat  they were filming in the middle of an  ocean in thailand  in weather that was excruciatingly hot  the mix of high waves and blazing sun  had the cast getting sick  over the side of the boat actor miguel  eran even had a heat stroke by the end  of it  we won't even touch on how awkward  filming the fifty shades of grey films  must have been but we're going to  discuss  what dakota johnson is claiming as one  of the toughest scenes to film  the elevator scene the elevator was  filled with the extras we see in the  final cut  but behind the cameras were 50 crew  members all confined to the tiny space  where dakota and jamie dornan got  quite intimate it is a kind of bizarre  experience andrew lincoln's first scene  of the entire walking dead series ended  up being his most  difficult to film it's the moment where  rick is faced with having to take down a  little zombie girl  that's when i realized this is going to  be the greatest job of my career but  also  the most painful this emotionally  bothered him so much that after a few  takes he was so distressed and  physically  needed to stop talk about nauseating  just what did leonardo dicaprio have to  go through in order to finally win an  oscar  well his time filming the revenant  wasn't pretty and it's difficult to pick  just one challenging thing he had to  endure on camera  from having to eat raw liver film with a  real bear and develop hypothermia  we're going to say leo wins for having  the most difficult time on set  i've never quite seen anything  cinematically like that  watching saul being kidnapped and forced  to dig his own grave was dark but behind  the scenes it was also grim  not only for saul's actor bob odenkirk  but for jesse and walt's actors brian  cranston and aaron paul  as well it was absolutely freezing on  location  and the winds were so strong the dirt  around them was blowing straight into  their faces  check out what walt had to say about the  scene i'm supposed to hold the gun out  and i'm so cold that i'm  shaking and i'm like oh my god that was  probably the toughest scene to do  he knew what he was talking about  charlize theron and zoe kravitz had a  lot to say about being on the set of mad  max including that filming the movie was  one of the hardest things they've ever  done  they were filming in conditions that  included extreme heat  beating sun dust storms and days that  went  way beyond your average eight hour work  day by the end of filming the cast was  exhausted from the difficult action  choreography  and dangerous car chases we don't blame  them  it was really fun who knew being an  actor could get this difficult  it's hard to believe how much the cast  and crew of these projects endured  just to bring us our favorite tv series  and films  we know they're getting paid really well  for their work but is it worth it  what do you think thanks for watching

